Parakeet model chain:

When Parakeet is selected, the ASR sidecar loads one artifact of `ggml-org/parakeet-GGUF` at
revision `35156454d1a39de06863303dd209fd2bed6ee079`. That revision holds two conversions of the
same checkpoint, and the app can be pointed at either:

- `ggml-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-f16.bin` — Parakeet's default variant
- `ggml-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-q8_0.bin` — the Compact selection

Both were converted from `nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3`, which is licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en. They are downloaded and cached at
runtime on first use of that backend; neither is bundled with the app or committed to this
repository.

NVIDIA does not endorse, sponsor or certify Voiceour.

Voiceour does not modify the weights. It loads a third-party format conversion of the
`nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3` checkpoint: `ggml-org/parakeet-GGUF` re-encoded that checkpoint
from NeMo into ggml, and quantised it for the `q8_0` artifact. Neither artifact is retrained
or fine-tuned. That conversion repository tags itself `license: mit`; a re-publisher cannot
relicense the checkpoint it converted, so CC BY 4.0 above is the licence that governs and this
